---
import Module10Behold from './Module10Behold';
import Module10Derive from './Module10Derive';
import Module10Operate from './Module10Operate';
import Module10Prompts from './Module10Prompts';
---

<div class="m m10">
  <section class="m-block m10-block">
    <p class="m-eyebrow">behold</p>
    <p>
      The spine has been hinting at this since Module 0. Schenker's
      claim: every well-formed tonal phrase has a deep structural
      skeleton — the <em>Ursatz</em> — which the surface elaborates
      through prolongation. Strip the elaborations off in layers and
      the skeleton appears. The chorale, reduced.
    </p>
    <Module10Behold client:visible />
  </section>

  <section class="m-block m10-block">
    <p class="m-eyebrow">derive</p>
    <p>
      Four layers. <strong>Foreground</strong> — every authored note.
      <strong>Middleground</strong> — chord tones survive, passing
      tones are absorbed. <strong>Background</strong> — one
      structural note per bar. <strong>Ursatz</strong> — three notes
      in the Urlinie, three in the Bassbrechung, the deep skeleton.
      Each layer is the previous one with one round of elaboration
      removed.
    </p>
    <Module10Derive client:visible />
  </section>

  <section class="m-block m10-block">
    <p class="m-eyebrow">operate</p>
    <p>
      Hear the layers. The harmonic arc is the same in all four
      tiers; only the elaborations change. The Ursatz strips the
      chorale to six notes and one cadence — and you can still hear
      that it cadenced.
    </p>
    <Module10Operate client:visible />
  </section>

  <section class="m-block m10-block">
    <p class="m-eyebrow">prompt</p>
    <p class="m-prompt-intro">
      Two cards on Schenker's depth model.
    </p>
    <Module10Prompts client:visible />
  </section>

  <section class="m-block m10-block m-bridge m10-bridge">
    <p class="m-eyebrow">bridge</p>
    <p>
      Schenker reveals tonality's static spine. But tonality{' '}
      <em>flows</em> — modulation is the order parameter shifting,
      consonance and dissonance are the field at thermal equilibrium
      or driven out of it. The final module sees music as active
      matter.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<style is:global>
  /* Module 10 specific rules. */

  .m10-behold,
  .m10-derive,
  .m10-operate {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .m10-staff-wrap {
    background: #f5efe0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem 0.2rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 400px;
  }
  .m10-staff {
    color: #1f1408;
    line-height: 0;
  }
  .m10-staff svg {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .m10-tier-track {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .m10-tier-step {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.65rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 3px;
    opacity: 0.45;
    transition:
      opacity 0.25s ease,
      border-color 0.25s ease,
      background 0.25s ease;
  }
  .m10-tier-step.active {
    opacity: 1;
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: rgba(232, 168, 56, 0.12);
  }
  .m10-tier-step-label {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .m10-tier-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .m10-tier-label {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .m10-tier-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .m10-tier-btn {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background 0.15s ease,
      color 0.15s ease,
      border-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .m10-tier-btn:hover:not(.active):not(:disabled) {
    border-color: var(--accent-dim);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .m10-tier-btn.active {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .m10-tier-btn:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .m10-operate-play {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.2rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .m10-operate-play:hover:not(:disabled) {
    background: var(--accent-dim);
    border-color: var(--accent-dim);
  }
  .m10-operate-play:disabled {
    cursor: default;
    background: var(--bg-button);
    color: var(--text-dim);
    border-color: var(--border);
  }
  .m10-behold-caption,
  .m10-derive-caption,
  .m10-operate-caption {
    font-size: 0.92rem !important;
    color: var(--text-dim) !important;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 !important;
    line-height: 1.55 !important;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }
  .m10-derive-caption strong {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .m10-behold-caption em,
  .m10-derive-caption em {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
